---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { ORG } from '../config';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../data/schema';
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy policy', href: '/privacy' }];
const N = '[needs your input]';
---
<Base title="Privacy policy (draft)" description="Draft privacy policy for Sugar Depth: camera and label photos, Google sign-in, Supabase, AI processing by Anthropic, on-device scan history and account deletion." path="/privacy" jsonLd={[breadcrumbs(crumbs)]}>
  <div class="wrap page-head">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <span class="kicker">Legal · draft</span>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap page-body prose">
    <div class="draft-note" role="note">
      <strong>Draft, not yet in effect.</strong> This policy has not been reviewed by a lawyer. Items marked <span class="needs">{N}</span> are facts that still need to be confirmed. Effective date: <span class="needs">{N}</span>.
    </div>

    <p>This policy explains what Sugar Depth (the scanner app and this website), operated by {ORG.name} in {ORG.locality}, Texas ("we"), collects and how it's used. Sugar Depth reads photos of food labels to flag added sugars and sweeteners.</p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <h3>Camera and label photos</h3>
    <p>The scanner uses your device camera only when you open it to photograph a label. Each photo is sent to our backend for reading. Photos of labels are not stored by us after the verdict is returned. <span class="needs">{N} Confirm that no photo is written to Supabase Storage, logs or any database.</span></p>
    <p>Please photograph only the label. If a photo includes people or other personal details, they are processed the same way.</p>
    <h3>Google sign-in</h3>
    <p>You sign in with Google. We receive your basic Google profile information, such as your name, email address and profile picture, to create your account. <span class="needs">{N} Confirm the exact Google OAuth scopes requested.</span></p>
    <h3>Account data</h3>
    <p>Your name and settings (preferences such as display options) are saved to your account. <span class="needs">{N} Confirm which fields are stored server-side.</span></p>
    <h3>Scan history</h3>
    <p>Your scan history (each verdict and the ingredient names found) is kept on your device only and is not sent to our servers.</p>
    <h3>This website</h3>
    <p>This marketing website uses no cookies and no analytics. <span class="needs">{N} Update if analytics are added.</span> Our host may keep standard server logs, such as IP address and browser type, for security.</p>

    <h2>Who processes your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> hosts our backend: authentication, account data and the functions that process each scan. <span class="needs">{N} Supabase project region.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Anthropic</strong> provides the AI model (Claude) that reads the ingredient text from your label photo. The photo is sent to Anthropic's API for this purpose. <span class="needs">{N} Confirm Anthropic's retention terms for your API account and whether data is used for training.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Verdict checker.</strong> <span class="needs">{N} The scanner also sends the photo to a third-party verdict service (Jev / TypeSafe, per the codebase). Name it here and describe its data handling, or remove this line if it is no longer used.</span></li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> provides sign-in.</li>
      <li><strong>Vercel</strong> hosts this website and the web version of the scanner.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We don't sell your personal information and don't use it for advertising.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>Account data is kept until you delete your account. <span class="needs">{N} Retention for server logs and backups.</span></p>

    <h2>Deleting your account</h2>
    <p>You can delete your account from the scanner's menu. This permanently deletes your profile from our servers and clears the scan history on your device. You can also email <a href={`mailto:${ORG.email}`}>{ORG.email}</a> to ask us to delete your data. <span class="needs">{N} Time frame for email deletion requests and backup purge.</span></p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>Sugar Depth is not directed to children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their information. <span class="needs">{N} Confirm the minimum age.</span></p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, including Texas under the Texas Data Privacy and Security Act, you may have rights to access, correct or delete your personal data. Email us to make a request. <span class="needs">{N} Lawyer review of state-law obligations.</span></p>

    <h2>Health information</h2>
    <p>Sugar Depth does not ask for health information, and its verdicts are not medical advice.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We'll post changes here and update the effective date.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>{ORG.name}, {ORG.locality}, Texas · <a href={`mailto:${ORG.email}`}>{ORG.email}</a> <span class="needs">{N} Mailing address, if you want one listed.</span></p>
  </div>
</Base>
